<http://data.silknow.org/object/10b01889-290b-3b7a-b9f6-397b559a3a65/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Vertical oval pendant, consisting of a frame of curved filigree scrolls surrounding an oval glass case containing a relic described as a piece of St Francis' sackcloth (<i>saccum</i>).  On the back is a red wax impression of an unknown cardinal's seal.  There is a ring for suspension made from a band of twisted wires at the top, resting on a filigree bead."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/10b01889-290b-3b7a-b9f6-397b559a3a65> .

